---- the coercion chain ----
42 -> float in [10,100]: ok=true
abc -> float: errors=1 code=8 (V_NOT_FLOAT=8)
7 -> int min 10: errors=1 code=10 (V_TOO_SMALL=10)
value out: 42 floatVal=2.5 boolVal=true
---- short-circuit: one error per chain ----
empty .required().minChars(3): errors=1 code=1 (V_REQUIRED=1)
...plus email(): errors=1 (still 1)
three failing rules: errors=1 code=3
---- required vs optional ----
  required on empty: errors=1 code=1 | a: is required
  optional on empty (rules suppressed): ok
  optional on present value (rules still run): errors=1 code=3 | c: must be at least 5 characters
  absent()=true ok()=true valueOr='fallback'
---- characters, not bytes ----
charCount: José=4 bytes=5  中文=2 bytes=6
José maxChars(4)=true maxBytes(4)=false
中文 exactChars(2)=true minBytes(6)=true
betweenChars: true/false
---- string rules ----
notBlank: false/true
trim then minChars: true
oneOf: true/false
oneOf message: must be one of: red, green
startsWith/endsWith/contains: truetruetruefalse
